A `.jsonc` file (JSON with comments, like `knip.jsonc`) is outlined by the JSON engine: its `//` header comment, and its keys, with the comment above `ignore` starting that key's line range and the trailing comma allowed.
== args
input/knip.jsonc
== file input/knip.jsonc
// Knip settings for the monorepo.
{
  "entry": ["src/index.ts"],
  // Generated code.
  "ignore": ["dist/**"],
}
== stdout
input/knip.jsonc (6 lines)
Knip settings for the monorepo.
